{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Ho.</b> A word of calling, like הוי כל צמא. These are the words of HaShem to the nations of the world: in those days, whoever wishes to learn Torah." "<b>And he who has no money.</b> The meaning: if he has no money to purchase, that he has no money to learn." "<b>Buy [and eat].</b> The meaning concerns wisdom, in the sense of אכול את המגילה הזאת (Ezekiel 3:1), for wisdom is to the soul like food to the body." "<b>And go.</b> To me." "<b>And the meaning: buy without money.</b> And eat without money. And the meaning of 'buy wine and milk': for both of them are like food and drink, and so the medical scholars acknowledge. And the meaning of 'wine and milk': for the Torah is likened to them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {4 "Bracketed editorial variant [צ״ל וטעם] before ושברו חנם rendered as 'the meaning' following the correction; bracketed text in the lemma [ואכלו] appears to be an editorial insertion completing the citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:37.625570061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}